  Every result lives at /?id=N, and there are 3,493 of them — but the site is
  client-rendered, so all 3,493 serve this same index.html byte for byte. The
  card is built by app.js after the catalogue loads. Listing them would offer a
  crawler thousands of URLs with identical markup, which is what duplicate
  content means. The root is the only distinct document there is.
-->
